    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3032" root="بَقَلَ" body-key="b">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَاقُولٌ</span></b> , (JK, A, O,) or ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بُوقَالٌ</span></b> , (K,) <i>A mug</i>
(<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كُوزٌ</span>) <i>having no</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُرْوَة</span> [or <i>handle</i>]; (JK, O, K;)
<i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كُوبٌ</span>: (A, TA:) [in Spanish <i>bokal,</i> (Golius,)
which favours the form in the K; but the Spanish
word may be from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بُوقَالَةٌ</span>, if from the Arabic:]
pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَوَاقِيلُ</span>. (JK, A, TA.)

